  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The graph of the cubic $y=P(x)$ has $x$-intercepts at $x=-2,0,2$ and passes through the point $(1,12)$. Determine $P(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=-4x(x-2)(x+2)$.",
      "worked": "By the Factor Theorem, the three intercepts give\n$$P(x)=ax(x-2)(x+2).$$\nUsing $P(1)=12$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a(1)(1-2)(1+2)&=12\\\\-3a&=12\\\\a&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$P(x)=-4x(x-2)(x+2).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
